P='<div style="margin-top:14px"><span class="tagh">Your analyst is involved</span></div>'
V1='<div class="jobsheet"><div><span>Question</span>What changed in the market, and does it matter for our decisions?</div><div><span>Scope</span>Six public sources, three competitors</div><div><span>Output</span>A one-page brief, dated and sourced</div></div>'
V2='<div class="rules"><div class="src"><div>Public sources</div><div>Customer documents</div><div>Customer numbers</div></div><div class="ar"></div><div class="rl"><h4>Agreed checks</h4><div>Every finding has a traceable source</div><div>Customer information and assumptions are labelled</div><div>Gaps are recorded as gaps</div></div><div class="ar"></div><div class="outb"><div style="background:var(--ambt);border-color:var(--amber)">Evidence set, ready to run</div></div></div><div style="margin-top:20px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid var(--rule)">'+lg4()+'</div>'
V3='<ul class="chk"><li><i class="ok"></i><div>Workflow configured on your sources<small>Rules, checks and output format agreed</small></div></li><li><i class="ok"></i><div>Tested against available historical data<small>Where suitable, compared with what actually happened</small></div></li><li><i class="pp"></i><div>First run checked by your analyst<small>Before anything reaches you</small></div></li><li><i></i><div>Ready to run on your schedule</div></li></ul><p class="vnote">Historical testing shows how a workflow handled known periods. It is not a forecast, and it does not guarantee future accuracy.</p>'
V4='<div class="pipe"><div><b>1</b><strong>Gather</strong>Read the agreed sources</div><div><b>2</b><strong>Date and source</strong>Attach both to each finding</div><div><b>3</b><strong>Apply checks</strong>Flag gaps and conflicts</div><div><b>4</b><strong>Draft</strong>Prepare the brief</div></div><div class="runs">On your agreed schedule, the same way every time. Gaps and exceptions go to the analyst, not into the brief as fact.</div>'
V5='<div class="memo2"><div class="h"><span>Weekly competitor brief</span><span class="tagh">Reviewed by a designated analyst</span></div><ul class="chk" style="padding:6px 18px"><li><i class="ok"></i><div>Source relevance checked</div></li><li><i class="ok"></i><div>Evidence traceable to a source</div></li><li><i class="ok"></i><div>Assumptions labelled</div></li><li><i class="pp"></i><div>Conflicting information flagged, not smoothed over<small>1 conflict flagged in this brief</small></div></li><li><i class="ok"></i><div>Interpretation reviewed and signed off</div></li></ul><div class="f">Delivered as a PDF or an email. The business decision stays yours. Illustrative.</div></div>'
